  "_comment": "WP8 — every public table with company_id is classified here. tests/integration/rls-matrix-coverage.test.ts FAILS if a company-scoped table is not classified, so a NEW sensitive table cannot ship on generic company-member write by omission. Classes: service_only (RPC/worker only), rpc_only (written only via a maker-checker/decision RPC), append_only (insert only), self_service (member inserts own row; capability updates), capability (operation-specific capability), identity (admin.identity.manage), company_member (lower-sensitivity operational/CRM; company-scoped write is the deliberate rule). As of migration 0048 (correction WP10) NO table is classified company_member: the commercially sensitive tables moved to capability, and WhatsApp history + worker notifications moved to service_only. See RLS_WRITE_POLICY_MATRIX.md. Promoted management kernel (migrations 0112-0141, classified 2026-09-11): 28 tables added. Each class was derived from the policies the table actually carries on a live database — service_only where RLS is on and no write policy exists, rpc_only where the write goes through one authority-checking RPC (assignment, completion claim, decision), capability where an INSERT/UPDATE policy names a has_capability() check. None is company_member.",
